      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-201",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "CVE-2026-92708: devalue 5.9.2 process memory disclosure via typed-array serialization (transitive via astro)\n\nThe dependency tree pinned by `bun.lock` contains **devalue 5.9.2**, which is affected by **CVE-2026-92708** (published advisory CVSS 7.5 HIGH): `stringify`/`uneval` serialize a typed array by emitting its entire backing `ArrayBuffer`, so serializing a Node `Buffer` (backing store is a process-wide shared pool) discloses up to 64 KB of unrelated process memory into the serialized output. Fixed in **5.9.3**. devalue is a transitive dependency pulled in by `astro@7.3.2` (`bun.lock:612`, dependency `\"devalue\": \"^5.8.1\"`; pinned at `bun.lock:778`). In this repository the exposure is minimal: the site is a fully prerendered static Astro build with no SSR server, and no project- or CMS-controlled data reaches the vulnerable typed-array serialization path."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "SECURITY.md"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "portfolio-astro",
                  "kind": "resource"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "a960dd8c3db6b474c12daae88bb268e460e684ee77715d1eb00e4c670de1ba7d"
          },
          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "1.9",
            "strix_vuln_class_hash": "fc5b00e78c014a47a8390bce1b8fc4544333403abf1bc24112a8843d95611c42",
            "synthetic_location": true,
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0001",
              "severity": "low",
              "cvss": 1.9,
              "timestamp": "2026-10-14 22:05:54 UTC",
              "target": "portfolio-astro",
              "cve": "CVE-2026-92708",
              "cwe": "CWE-201",
              "impact": "Build-process memory disclosure: if a Node Buffer or typed array were passed through devalue serialization during `astro build`, up to 64 KB of build-process memory (potentially including build env such as `CONTENT_API_KEY`/`GHOST_URL` set in the Docker build stage) would be emitted into published static output. In this codebase no Buffer/typed-array data is serialized and no long-running multi-request SSR process exists, so no disclosure was demonstrated; the pinned version nonetheless keeps the vulnerable code in the build toolchain.",
              "technical_analysis": "**Version verification.** `bun.lock:778` pins `devalue@5.9.2`; the advisory affects 5.1.0–5.9.2 and fixes 5.9.3, so the pin is in the affected range. Trivy (vuln DB refreshed at scan time, 2026-10-14) matched it from `bun.lock`.\n\n**Source-to-sink trace (this codebase).**\n- Entry point: lockfile pin `bun.lock:778` + direct dependency `astro: ^7.3.2` at `package.json:26`; astro requires `\"devalue\": \"^5.8.1\"` (`bun.lock:612`).\n- Usage sites of devalue inside astro 7.3.2 (`node_modules/astro/dist`): `content/vite-plugin-content-imports.js`, `content/data-store.js`, `content/data-store-writer.js`, `content/mutable-data-store.js` (content collections), `actions/runtime/server.js` + `actions/runtime/client.js` (server actions), `core/session/runtime.js` (sessions), `core/errors/errors-data.js`. \n- None of these paths are active in this project: there is no `src/content/` directory (no content collections — blog content is fetched at build time via `@tryghost/content-api` in `src/lib/ghost.ts:14`), no server actions (output is fully static), and no Astro session usage.\n- The only hydrated islands are `DarkModeToggle` and `FxToggle` with `client:load` and no props (`src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro:80`, `src/components/base/Header.astro:39,45`); the built HTML carries literal `props=\"{}\"` (verified in `dist/index.html`), so no devalue-serialized payload — typed array or otherwise — is produced or shipped. No `devalue` markers were found in any `dist/_astro/*.js` client bundle.\n- The CVE's canonical scenario (SvelteKit/Nuxt-style SSR where a public `load()` returns a small Buffer, disclosed across in-flight requests in a long-running process) requires a multi-request server, which this static nginx deployment does not have.\n\n**Counterevidence pass.** Checked: all astro dist consumers of devalue (listed above), all project source imports (no `devalue` import anywhere in `src/`), island props in built output (`{}`), client bundles (no devalue parse runtime shipped), and absence of SSR. The only remaining theoretical trigger is an operator placing a Buffer/typed array into island or content-collection props — a developer-position action, not an attacker path.\n\n**Environment caveat.** External advisory lookup (web search) was unavailable in this scan; verification relies on the Trivy vulnerability database downloaded fresh from `mirror.gcr.io/aquasec/trivy-db:2` at scan time plus its embedded advisory references (GHSA-j22f-vq7h-c4qm, sveltejs/devalue commit 46dc877b).",
              "remediation_steps": "Refresh the lockfile so the transitive resolution moves devalue to the fixed release: run `bun update devalue` (astro's range `^5.8.1` accepts 5.9.3, so no manifest change is required). If a future astro release re-pins or the resolution stays stale, add a root-level `overrides` entry pinning `devalue` to `^5.9.3` in package.json. Also apply the sibling fixes bundled in devalue 5.9.3 (six GHSA-only advisories covering uneval expansion, ArrayBuffer-reviver validation, unhandled stringifyAsync rejection, `__proto__` key coercion, and sparse-array amplification — not separately filed because they have no CVE IDs). Re-run `bun run build` and confirm the lockfile records `devalue@5.9.3`.",
              "dependency_metadata": {
                "package_name": "devalue",
                "installed_version": "5.9.2",
                "advisory_cvss": 7.5,
                "package_ecosystem": "npm",
                "manifest_path": "bun.lock",
                "fixed_version": "5.9.3",
                "introduced_by": "astro@7.3.2",
                "dependency_path": "astro@7.3.2 > devalue@5.9.2",
                "reachability": "imported",
                "reachability_evidence": "devalue is not imported by application code (no `devalue` reference anywhere under `src/`); it enters only through the direct dependency `astro@7.3.2` (package.json:26, bun.lock:612 requires `\"devalue\": \"^5.8.1\"`, pin at bun.lock:778), which is used on every build (`bun run build`). The vulnerable symbols (stringify/uneval typed-array serialization) appear in astro's dist consumers at node_modules/astro/dist/content/{vite-plugin-content-imports.js,data-store.js,data-store-writer.js,mutable-data-store.js}, node_modules/astro/dist/actions/runtime/{server.js,client.js}, and node_modules/astro/dist/core/session/runtime.js — but none of those subsystems are active in this project: no src/content/ directory exists, the build output is fully static (no server actions, no sessions), and the two client:load islands (src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro:80, src/components/base/Header.astro:39,45) serialize literal empty props (`props=\"{}\"` in dist/index.html). The specific vulnerable behavior (serializing a Node Buffer/typed array) is never exercised with any data, attacker- or operator-controlled, and no devalue runtime ships in dist/_astro/*.js.",
                "contextual_cvss_breakdown": {
