          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "CVE-2026-93748: http-cache-semantics 4.2.0 cross-user cache disclosure via max-stale (transitive via astro)\n\nThe `bun.lock` tree pins **http-cache-semantics 4.2.0**, affected by **CVE-2026-93748** (published advisory CVSS 7.5 HIGH): when processing client `max-stale` directives the library fails to properly validate security-zeroed cache entries, letting unauthenticated attackers retrieve cached responses belonging to other users (e.g. another user's `Set-Cookie` credentials) from a shared cache. The advisory covers all versions through 4.2.0 and no fixed release is listed. The package is transitive via `astro@7.3.2` (`bun.lock:612`, `\"http-cache-semantics\": \"^4.2.0\"`; pin at `bun.lock:900`). This deployment has no shared cache, no per-user server responses, and never loads the sole consumer module, so the published rating does not carry over to this codebase."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
