              "target": "portfolio-astro",
              "cve": "CVE-2026-93748",
              "cwe": "CWE-524",
              "impact": "No impact demonstrated in this codebase. The vulnerable behavior would allow cross-user disclosure of cached HTTP responses (including session cookies) from a shared cache; here the only consumer is astro's build-time remote-image caching, the project uses no remote images, and the site serves identical static files to every visitor, so there are no per-user cached responses and no attacker-reachable cache query path. Risk is latent: a future feature that enables remote images or server-side/shared caching would pull this code into an active path while the version remains unfixed upstream.",
              "technical_analysis": "**Version verification.** `bun.lock:900` pins `http-cache-semantics@4.2.0`; the advisory states \"through 4.2.0\" with no fixed version, so the pin is affected. Trivy (DB refreshed 2026-10-14 at scan time) matched it from `bun.lock`.\n\n**Source-to-sink trace (this codebase).**\n- Entry point: lockfile pin `bun.lock:900`; direct dependency `astro: ^7.3.2` at `package.json:26`; astro requires `\"http-cache-semantics\": \"^4.2.0\"` (`bun.lock:612`).\n- Sole consumer in the entire locked tree: `node_modules/astro/dist/assets/build/remote.js:1` — imported and used at :15/:50 to construct `new CachePolicy(webToCachePolicyRequest(req), webToCachePolicyResponse(res))` for build-time remote image fetches. The request object is generated by the build itself (`webToCachePolicyRequest({url, method, headers})` at :66); no `maxStale` option is ever passed.\n- This project never exercises that module: `src/` contains no `astro:assets`, `<Image>`, or `getImage` usage, so `astro build` performs no remote image fetching.\n- The Ghost content fetch (`src/lib/ghost.ts:14`) goes through `@tryghost/content-api`, whose only declared dependency is axios 1.20.0 — a separate HTTP stack not covered by this CVE.\n- The deployed site is static files served by nginx: there is no application-level HTTP cache, no per-user responses, and no endpoint where an attacker can send a `max-stale` directive.\n\n**Counterevidence pass.** Verified the consumer set exhaustively (dependency map across all 620 locked packages; only astro imports the package), confirmed the consumer module is dead code for this configuration (no remote images), and confirmed the Ghost fetch stack is independent (axios). The theoretical residual — enabling remote images later while the version stays unfixed — would still only affect the build's local image cache, not a multi-user shared cache.\n\n**Environment caveat.** Web search was unavailable; advisory identity and the \"no fixed version\" status were taken from the Trivy DB refreshed on scan day plus embedded references (Red Hat CVE page, upstream issue #56, VulnCheck advisory).",
              "remediation_steps": "No fixed release exists upstream at scan time. Track kornelski/http-cache-semantics issue #56 and bump via `bun update http-cache-semantics` (or a root package.json `overrides` entry pinning the first fixed version) once a release lands; astro's range `^4.2.0` will accept it. Also upgrade `astro` when a release ships with the fixed dependency. As defense in depth, avoid enabling astro remote-image fetching or any server-side/shared response caching for this site without first confirming the dependency has been fixed; if remote images are ever introduced, verify no cache is shared across users.",
              "dependency_metadata": {
                "package_name": "http-cache-semantics",
                "installed_version": "4.2.0",
                "advisory_cvss": 7.5,
                "package_ecosystem": "npm",
                "manifest_path": "bun.lock",
                "fixed_version": "none published",
                "introduced_by": "astro@7.3.2",
                "dependency_path": "astro@7.3.2 > http-cache-semantics@4.2.0",
                "reachability": "imported",
                "reachability_evidence": "http-cache-semantics is not imported by application code; it enters only through the direct dependency `astro@7.3.2` (package.json:26; bun.lock:612 requires `\"http-cache-semantics\": \"^4.2.0\"`, pin at bun.lock:900). A full-tree dependency map over all 620 locked packages found exactly one consumer: `node_modules/astro/dist/assets/build/remote.js:1` (`import CachePolicy from \"http-cache-semantics\"`), used at :15 and :50-52 to build policies from the build's own request/response objects (`webToCachePolicyRequest` at :66 never sets maxStale). That module is the build-time remote-image fetcher; this project contains zero remote-image usage (`rg 'astro:assets|<Image|getImage' src/` → no hits), so the module is never loaded during `astro build`. The Ghost CMS fetch uses `@tryghost/content-api` whose only runtime dependency is axios 1.20.0 (`node_modules/@tryghost/content-api/package.json`), not http-cache-semantics. The vulnerable behavior additionally requires attacker-supplied `max-stale` request directives against a multi-user shared cache — a component that does not exist in this static nginx deployment.",
                "contextual_cvss_breakdown": {
                  "attack_complexity": "H",
                  "attack_vector": "L",
                  "availability": "N",
                  "confidentiality": "N",
                  "integrity": "N",
                  "privileges_required": "H",
                  "scope": "U",
                  "user_interaction": "N"
                },
                "contextual_cvss_score": 0.0,
                "contextual_cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:N",
                "contextual_cvss_reasoning": "The published 7.5 (AV:N/PR:N/C:H) assumes an internet-facing shared HTTP cache holding other users' responses (e.g. session cookies) that an unauthenticated attacker can query with `max-stale`. In this codebase no such component exists: the only consumer of http-cache-semantics in the whole 620-package tree is astro's build-time remote-image module `node_modules/astro/dist/assets/build/remote.js:1` (constructed at :15 and :50 from build-generated request/response objects with no maxStale option), that module is never loaded because the project uses no remote images (zero `astro:assets`/`<Image>`/`getImage` references under `src/`), and the Ghost content fetch goes through `@tryghost/content-api` → axios 1.20.0 (`src/lib/ghost.ts:14`), not through this cache. The deployed artifact is static files behind nginx with no per-user server responses to cache. Consequently every impact metric is N in this codebase: the vulnerable max-stale validation path exists in the build toolchain but has no attacker-reachable instance and no sensitive cached data; the advisory score is retained as the published reference only."
              }
